    status: "in_corpus",
    priority: "critical",
    symbol: "🌑",
    card_image: "https://gallica.bnf.fr/iiif/ark:/12148/bpt6k15122214/f11/full/400,/0/native.jpg",
    card_description: "The Mutus Liber ('Silent Book,' La Rochelle, 1677) is the most enigmatic work in alchemical iconography: 15 plates with almost no text, depicting an alchemist and his female partner performing the complete work — gathering dew, heating vessels, observing celestial signs — from first matter to the Stone. All 15 plates now accessible via BnF Gallica IIIF.",
